WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.364
Run History

00:00:01.482 --> 00:00:02.460
an indie iPhone

00:00:02.272 --> 00:00:02.767
app

00:00:03.294 --> 00:00:04.532
Thomas Hanning shipped

00:00:04.344 --> 00:00:05.298
Run History

00:00:05.499 --> 00:00:06.926
a SwiftUI iPhone

00:00:06.737 --> 00:00:07.645
app that turns

00:00:07.457 --> 00:00:08.270
a whole running

00:00:08.082 --> 00:00:09.579
career across watches

00:00:09.414 --> 00:00:11.088
into on-device statistics

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.362
and fitness trends

00:00:12.886 --> 00:00:13.829
The app compares

00:00:13.641 --> 00:00:14.678
this week month

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:15.385
and year against

00:00:15.197 --> 00:00:16.317
the same period

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:16.919
last year

00:00:17.002 --> 00:00:18.345
tracks yearly goals

00:00:18.157 --> 00:00:19.466
and weekly streaks

00:00:19.289 --> 00:00:20.515
and finds best

00:00:20.339 --> 00:00:21.753
efforts across every

00:00:21.565 --> 00:00:22.650
watch you've owned

00:00:23.174 --> 00:00:24.164
Hanning says its

00:00:23.976 --> 00:00:25.190
core package builds

00:00:25.002 --> 00:00:25.992
and tests on

00:00:25.804 --> 00:00:26.971
Linux and most

00:00:26.782 --> 00:00:27.454
of the code

00:00:27.266 --> 00:00:28.091
was written with

00:00:27.903 --> 00:00:28.763
Claude Code in

00:00:28.575 --> 00:00:29.270
the cloud

00:00:29.507 --> 00:00:30.650
his write-up covers

00:00:30.462 --> 00:00:31.181
how he built

00:00:30.992 --> 00:00:31.428
it

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:32.964
Full story on

00:00:32.775 --> 00:00:33.671
the dashboard
